WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.416
transform tests the sign of each lane’s value.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:07.604
Negative values are negated; the other path doubles its values.

00:00:07.824 --> 00:00:16.123
All 32 threads belong to one warp. alternateSigns in main changes the input signs, rather than the kernel’s branch condition.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:19.295
Test signs.

00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:22.587
Each lane evaluates value < 0.0f.

00:00:22.807 --> 00:00:24.044
Execute paths.

00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:27.080
Only participating lanes update their outputs.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.324
Continue.

00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:30.464
The warp proceeds after the branch.

00:00:32.484 --> 00:00:35.151
A warp instruction has participating lanes.

00:00:35.371 --> 00:00:38.763
Different branch paths can require different active lane sets.

00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:44.700
These lanes are logical positions in a warp, not a drawing of separate dedicated processors.
